# Phase 9 Rev 1 M1: the stock files the shell keeps for developer mode
# (menu.c, debug_menu.c, screens.c, gui/list.c) still work with the trims
# on. Every debug screen of the simulator build opens and closes in turn:
# no crash, no other splash. With IPODUI_TRIM_SKIN the stock lists draw
# unthemed, full screen (no skinned status bar); IPODUI_TRIM_VOICE drops
# "Talk engine stats" and IPODUI_TRIM_SKIN "Skin Engine RAM usage" (their
# engines are gone). The simulator's list is five rows: View OS stacks,
# Screendump, Metadata log, View database info, View buffering thread.
# The device has more (I/O ports, PCF registers, CPU frequency, battery,
# HW info, partitions, disk info): a P10 device check. Screendump and
# Metadata log are toggles whose stock "... enabled/disabled" splash passes
# in developer mode by design (8a M3, as before P9); each is toggled twice
# so the settings end as found.
#   SIM_BUILD=build/sim-ui scripts/shots.sh tests/ui/ipodui-p9-devmode-debug.script
# needs: library
# trace: devmode
# log: devmode enter
# log: devmode exit
# env: SIM_TRACE_LCD_PUSH=1
# logbetween: dev_in dev_shown \bsim lcd push x=0 y=0 w=320 h=240\b
# golden: skip debug os_stacks screendump metadata_log db_info buffering about_after

wait 5000            # boot
wheel +3            # Settings (4th main-menu row)
wait 400
key SELECT          # Settings; About is its first row
wait 1500
key SELECT          # About
wait 1500
ab_mark dev_in      # #63: the device showed About through all of this
chord SELECT+LEFT 3200
wait 1000
wheel -2            # Advanced (above Back; the list wraps)
wait 400
key SELECT
wait 800
wheel -1            # System debug (its last row)
wait 400
key SELECT          # System debug
wait 1000
shot debug
ab_mark dev_shown   # the Developer and Debug lists reached the panel

key SELECT          # 1 View OS stacks
wait 1500
shot os_stacks
key LEFT
wait 800
wheel +1
wait 300
key SELECT          # 2 Screendump: a toggle, back in the list at once
wait 1500
key SELECT          # toggled back
wait 1500
shot screendump
wheel +1
wait 300
key SELECT          # 3 Metadata log: a toggle too
wait 1500
key SELECT          # toggled back
wait 1500
shot metadata_log
wheel +1
wait 300
key SELECT          # 4 View database info
wait 1500
shot db_info
key LEFT
wait 800
wheel +1
wait 300
key SELECT          # 5 View buffering thread
wait 1500
shot buffering
key LEFT
wait 800

key LEFT            # out of Debug, to Advanced
wait 800
key LEFT            # Advanced
wait 600
key LEFT            # Developer, on Advanced
wait 600
wheel +1            # the Back row
wait 400
key SELECT          # Back: leave developer mode
wait 1500
shot about_after
quit
